WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.480
Thanks!

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.540
It's so sweet!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.050
<i>It all began that winter evening.</i>

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.270
If you don't have anyone, then maybe I can...

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.180
Maybe I can be your family!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.690
<i>Every Saturday, Kirin arrives.</i>

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.700
<i>At night, Ryo cooks dinner.</i>

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.580
<i>On Sunday morning, we go to cram school together.</i>

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.580
<i>Good food and good times...</i>

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.710
<i>Week after week...</i>

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.710
<i>And soon...</i>

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.290
<i>It'll be spring.</i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.050
...and a cherry tomato to liven it up.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:50.940
There we go.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.400
It's a great day for flower viewing!

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.950
There you are, Kirin.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.740
You brought a lot of things again.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.240
I've got everything we need for a picnic!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.240
A blanket for when it gets cold!

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.160
A flashlight in case we drop something! Everything!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.170
I don't think we'll be needing any of those...

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.590
Anyway, I'm not quite ready yet.
Do you mind waiting inside for a bit?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.550
No problem!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.430
Oh, wow, you cooked! Tons!

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.390
Yep. I worked real hard on them.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.020
I can't wait!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.400
I made some too, just like I promised.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.070
Wanna see? Well?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.360
It's flat white...

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.660
Oh, that's just the top.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:44.910
See?

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.960
Oh, you made sandwiches?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.420
Yeah. I woke up early, and Daddy helped me out.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.090
Why is the bread all soggy?!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.430
You have to spread the margarine before you add the lettuce.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.140
Is this all you're using?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.890
<i>Boring</i>.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.020
Says the woman who cooks nothing but veggie stir-fry.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.980
C'mon, you kids are going to a festival.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.980
You've gotta kick it up a notch.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.400
See? Spread it on nice and thick, like this.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.650
That's a <i>lot</i> of mustard!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.860
Mom's gone mad.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.160
So picking your sandwiches will kinda be like a game of Russian roulette,

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.040
but don't worry too hard about it!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.330
Sounds exciting...

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.960
I'm glad you've patched things up with your mom.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.880
It's because of that hot pot recipe you gave me when I left.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.260
But you're the one who made it.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:51.020
Well, it wasn't the hot pot itself.
It was how carefully you wrote the recipe.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.140
She was relieved by how mature you are.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.440
Oh, we can see it from here!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.290
This is amazing, Ryo!

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.380
I've never seen this many cherry blossoms in one place!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.050
Watch your step, Kirin!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.970
Let's spread our blanket here.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.730
Okay!

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:40.020
Weigh down the corners with our bags so it doesn't blow around, and...

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.770
There!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.400
This is really the real thing!

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.240
It's just like I saw on TV!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.080
Now we just have to wait for Akira.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.370
Oh, that's right. Akira's coming too.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:02.880
Yep. She said she'll be here at around five,
after she finishes up at work.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.220
Kirin? Why are you shivering like that?

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.340
I-I've never met Akira in person before.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.350
I get really nervous when meeting grownups for the first time.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.350
I-I'm not gonna make a bad impression, right?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.690
Are my bangs okay?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.440
You look really cute.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:26.860
Akira's really friendly. You don't have anything to worry about.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.700
O-Okay...

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.160
Look, there she is!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.290
Ryo! Long time no see!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.580
Hi, Akira!

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.790
Um...

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.290
I missed you so much!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:40.540
Me too—

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.590
Sorry for leaving you alone for so long!

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.340
Here, have some sakura mochi!

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.390
What are you doing...

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.180
So this is how adults behave together...

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.560
Ah, you must be Kirin!

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.770
Yes.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.320
Nice to meet you. I'm Machiko Akira.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.440
I'm Morino Kirin.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:12.030
I'm really sorry for crashing your date!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.330
How cute!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.290
You're really as polite as I've heard you are!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.790
<i>She's acting completely different.</i>

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:27.210
Now that we're all here, let's see what we've brought!

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:30.930
I can't wait to taste your cooking again!

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.260
What did you bring, Akira?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.930
You <i>did</i> bring something, right?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.310
We're at a fair! We should have fair food!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.190
So...

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.700
you want us to go buy something?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:08:00.040
You're right, Ryo. Akira's a nice person.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.000
Isn't she?

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:07.420
I'm surprised that you'd be acting so differently, though...

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.630
What's in those bags, Ryo?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.890
They've got cute characters printed on them!

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.050
It's cotton candy.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.100
Cool!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.680
Look at it fluff up!

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.600
Kirin!

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.310
What are these?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.980
Sugar sculptures.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.990
It's a really delicate craft...

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.740
Huh?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.240
Pink and blue bananas!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.160
They look super unhealthy.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.990
I'm sorry!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.410
Have you not seen a chocolate-dipped banana before?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.420
Wait, is this your first time at a fair?

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.170
At a real one, yeah.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.170
A "real one"?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.090
Yeah.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.180
In my neighborhood, we just have a local street fair.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.430
With things like shaved ice, and yakisoba.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.310
The kids make the tickets for the raffle,

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.060
and the prizes are whatever people bring.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.730
That sounds fun.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.770
You know everything about fairs, Ryo!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.690
E-Everything?

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:16.740
Not really. I only visit during this festival.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.530
Is it a tradition?

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.740
Yep.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.750
Lately I've missed a couple,

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.040
but when I was little, I came every year.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.920
We all cooked together.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.630
It was so much fun.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.680
Every year, I looked forward to spring coming.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.860
I never knew...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.240
Of course not.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.700
I've never told you before, right?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:03.990
Me too!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.500
I want to make you happy too!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:15.010
I mean... We <i>are</i> family...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:18.180
Make a sketch of me looking awesome.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.140
That's...

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.310
Am I swag enough?

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.520
Take your shirt off!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.890
The necktie headband's a nice touch.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.150
For real? Sweet!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.770
Shiina?

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.410
The heck did those two get off to?

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.330
Guess it's okay for me to take a nibble...

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.330
What the...

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.500
it's all white!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.460
Oh, Machiko.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.880
What are you doing, Shiina?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.470
Hm? Just sketching some people.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.010
I'm done. Here you go.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.890
Thanks a bunch!

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:04.850
What d'ya reckon?

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.100
Better than reality for sure!

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.350
People? Not the cherry blossoms?

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:15.480
Sure. Drawing grownups is loads of fun.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.030
Did you come alone?

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.740
Yeah, how about you?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.610
I'm with my cousin.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.210
Oh, it's that grade-schooler you've been bringing to cram school!

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.750
Actually, we're the same age.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.170
Oh, my bad.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.500
I'm Shiina. Nice to meet you.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.840
Morino Kirin.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:44.890
See, Kirin? You've made another friend in Tokyo!

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.770
You're acting completely different than you do at school, Machiko.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.520
Really?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.150
You're usually super-focused.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:57.730
Peas and carrots, peas and carrots...

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.860
People avoid you in case it's contagious.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.410
No way...

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.620
I never knew...

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.620
Well, we go to different classes.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.000
I guess you don't know what she brings for lunch either?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.750
Her lunch?!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.090
They're great. Especially her rolled omelettes.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.880
She always shares them with me.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:26.430
I just worry about you since you always bring just a rice ball.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.890
<i>It's like I don't know anything about Ryo...</i>

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.980
I'm probably the only one who knows how they taste.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.070
Excuse me!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.240
I've eaten lots of Ryo's cooking too!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.360
Kirin?

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.910
When I was lonely, she made me hot pot!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.540
When I had a cold, she made homemade kitsune udon!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.250
Sometimes it's like having another grandma!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.340
Especially when she puts sugar on the pickled plums—

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.460
That's enough now!

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.930
I see how special she is to you.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.770
Here, take this. As an apology.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.140
What is this?

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.390
Candy.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.810
Anyway, toodles.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.770
You're leaving already?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.110
I've had enough sketching old men for one day.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.400
It's time to go stuff my face.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.410
Draw it all, then eat it all.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.160
You should sketch the flowers too.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.910
Shouldn't you go catch up with her?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:38.290
Why? I'm here with you today, Kirin.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.300
Right...

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.380
Aren't you lucky? She gave you a candy apple.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.420
Yeah.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.180
It's so beautiful up close.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:55.060
<i>I tried to act all grown up by telling Ryo I'd be her family,</i>

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.060
<i>but there's still so much I don't know about her...</i>

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:04.280
<i>It's like everyone knows her better than I do.</i>

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.860
Do you like it?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.740
Yeah. It's sweet... and a little sour.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.250
Sorry we kept you waiting, Akira.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.760
It's so hot!

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.640
What's wrong, Akira?!

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.930
What did you do to that sandwich, Ryo!?

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.310
My nose is burning!

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:38.940
Oh, you must've gotten the Russian roulette sandwich.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.650
It's your own fault for trying to sneak a bite.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:46.150
Anyway, we've waited too long. Let's dig in.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:49.030
For starters, we've got rice balls, fried chicken, and potato salad.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:52.870
There's also takoyaki, grilled squid,
and corn on the cob.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.700
Amazing! It's like I'm at a three-star Michelin restaurant!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:01.580
Everyone, a toast!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.340
Cheers!

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:17.350
The taste of the salted rice is filling my whole mouth...

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.480
<i>Thick squid with the aroma of teriyaki sauce...</i>

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.530
<i>I don't know if I can keep from drooling on myself!</i>

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.780
<i>The sweetness!</i>

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:39.290
<i>The crispy roastedness!
The soy sauce glaze! I can't stop!</i>

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.290
This is just too good!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.090
Kirin?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.210
Ryo...

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.840
Why didn't you make rolled omelettes?

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:56.350
Never mind, I think I'll try the takoyaki now!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:59.270
That's right! Go for it!

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.110
That was great. Lots of fun too.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:09.400
All right! Time to go back to work!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.110
After drinking like that?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:15.070
That's just enough to keep me fueled!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.240
See ya!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.120
Looks like Akira had fun.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.660
I guess so.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:26.040
Bath's ready, Kirin.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.710
It was pretty chilly today. You should warm up in the...

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:32.470
Kirin?

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.680
Wh-What?

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.930
Are you not feeling well?

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.060
I'm fine!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.560
I was just thinking about how much fun today was.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.060
I wish we had a bit more time.
I wanted to sketch the flowers too!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.440
Why don't we do that now?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.440
Huh?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.990
Where are you going, Ryo?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.210
We only have this one, but...

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:10.920
Oh yeah, it was blossoming here too!

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.460
It's beautiful!

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.130
It's special when we go to the park,

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.890
but Grandma and I usually just stayed right here.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:22.600
This is great! I can draw as much as I want!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.770
You get started on your sketch.
I'll be back in a minute.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.820
I wonder where Ryo went?

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:45.620
Kirin!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.170
Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.960
Ready for round two?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:03.180
I made rolled omelettes, just like the ones I bring to school.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.940
Ryo...

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.030
Thanks!

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:24.490
It's so sweet!

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:25.910
Is it too sweet?

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.210
No, I love it like this!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.960
It's sweet, but I can still taste the broth.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.470
It's, like, really delicate.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:38.470
I'm glad you like it.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:42.140
I thought I was stuffed, but I can't stop eating.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.230
Wow, this one has cheese!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.940
You found it.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.610
I wanted to try something kind of like your Russian roulette sandwich.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.690
Thanks.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.660
And sorry.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.370
Why are you apologizing?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.870
I made you worry, right?

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.870
Kirin...

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:13.460
I saw an entirely different side of you today.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.880
I felt a little surprised...

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.380
and isolated...

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.640
Me too.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:27.310
I learned a lot about you today too.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:31.600
I never knew you were so shy around grownups.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:36.610
Or that you'd never been to a fair.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:42.110
But I'm happy. The more I learn about you,

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:46.370
the more I feel like we're getting closer together.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.670
Me too.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:54.460
Yep.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:20:00.550
I felt a little lonely, but I'm so glad I got to know you better!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.930
I told you I hate carrots, right?

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:16.230
They smell fishy, and I don't like how the word "carrot" sounds.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.860
It just makes me really not want to eat them.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.280
That's certainly an unusual reason.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.110
I'll be sure to remember, though.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.030
<i>Since we've just met...</i>

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.200
Are there any foods you don't like?

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.950
Let's see...

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.580
I guess I'm not a fan of avocados.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.830
<i>There's still so much we don't know.</i>

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.590
<i>Even though we've just met...</i>

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:42.010
I used to be shy only around grownup men.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.510
Only men?

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:47.430
I have an uncle who's super-duper loud.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:51.180
Since my Dad's so quiet, he used to terrify me.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:54.520
Oh, I remember him.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.400
What was his name... Ryozo?

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.820
Yeah! Uncle Ryozo!

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.360
<i>We already know so much.</i>

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:09.120
I'm just glad I figured out what I really wanted to know.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:15.120
I want to see what your art is like!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.960
I-I'm not even done yet!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.000
So what?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.170
No! No way!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:23.510
<i>Yes. From here on...</i>

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.550
<i>We'll get to understand each other better than anyone else.</i>

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:32.430
Where'd I put my card...

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:34.310
I'll hold that.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.600
Found it!

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.940
See you next week!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:42.610
Yep, next week.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.200
Wait, Kirin, your...

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:52.330
Next week should be fine.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:59.580
I thought Kirin's style would be vivid and bold,

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:07.010
but it's really delicate and gentle.

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:44.400
So, Kirin, do you like it wrapped around or laid on top?

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.070
Laid on top, of course!

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:51.950
If you do it that way, you can just make a little cut and all the insides come running out.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:58.830
Then you take all that sticky stuff and blend it right in...

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:03.080
That could have sounded a bit more appetizing...

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:06.000
Next time, on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.920
Rich and Crispy!
